{"chapter": "spaces-groupoids", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "0439", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\Sch_{fppf}$", "MATH_0002": "$A$", "MATH_0003": "$\\Spec(A)$", "MATH_0004": "$S$", "MATH_0005": "$X$", "MATH_0006": "$S$", "MATH_0007": "$X \\times_S X$", "MATH_0008": "$X$", "MATH_0009": "$S$", "MATH_0010": "$X \\times X$", "MATH_0011": "$0$", "MATH_0012": "$\\text{pr}_0 : X \\times_S Y \\to X$", "MATH_0013": "$\\text{pr}_1 : X \\times_S Y \\to Y$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent", "STRUCT_0002": "\\medskip", "STRUCT_0003": "\\noindent", "STRUCT_0004": "\\medskip", "STRUCT_0005": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:5a402f3445ba76d1843e12defcbacdd1c075bbb54d7fb434d9d33c515f076eb7", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:e877bb45545ee0fd13f60b715cd1b1b7a58648efc10f8fd7fd038a190f65216c", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nThe standing assumption is that all schemes are contained in\na big fppf site <MATH_0001>. And all rings <MATH_0002> considered\nhave the property that <MATH_0003> is (isomorphic) to an\nobject of this big site.\n\n<STRUCT_0002><STRUCT_0003>\nLet <MATH_0004> be a scheme and let <MATH_0005> be an algebraic space over <MATH_0006>.\nIn this chapter and the following we will write <MATH_0007>\nfor the product of <MATH_0008> with itself (in the category of algebraic\nspaces over <MATH_0009>), instead of <MATH_0010>.\n\n<STRUCT_0004><STRUCT_0005>\nWe continue our convention to label projection maps starting with\nindex <MATH_0011>, so we have <MATH_0012> and\n<MATH_0013>.\n\n\n\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:ab382693b1830230467a95331caee64c8fac1fdebfd3cbc5db63b726dc3d2e66", "unit_id": "tag:0439:prose-0001"}
